 "title": "Comparative Analysis of Gene Prediction Tools and Sequencing Technologies",
 "summary": "This cluster focuses on gene prediction tools and their performance on simulated data. BRAKER2 is highlighted as a top performer, outperforming TSEBRA and BRAKER1 in terms of accuracy and F1 score. StringTie2 is also shown to be faster and more accurate than FLAIR and Scallop. The cluster also includes various sequencing technologies, including PacBio and Illumina, which are used to generate simulated data. Additionally, the cluster includes organisms such as Homo sapiens, Drosophila melanogaster, and mus musculus, which have orthologs with each other. The MAKER pipeline uses several of these tools, including BRAKER2, RepeatMasker, and StringTie.",
